This is a 15-bit struct. When you do `*reinterpret_cast<Color555 *>(src)`, it reads 2 bytes. The struct has 15 bits of fields. The 16th bit (bit 15) is padding. When MSAN checks the read of `c.r`, `c.g`, `c.b`, it reads 5 bits each. If the 2 bytes are fully initialized, no issue.

